// A `paths` key may be a module prefix — koru.json has accepted
// `"vend/pkg": "./lib"` since longestAliasMatch landed (src/module_resolver.zig:
// "koru/vaxis beats koru", segment-boundary matching). The source-level
// directive refuses the same key, and its refusal text cites the premise the
// longest match falsified: "every use site splits on the first /". Two
// spellings of one declaration, one refusing what the other accepts.
// Red today: KORU172 on the paths block. Green when source-level aliases get
// the grammar koru.json already has (isUsableModulePrefix exists for it).

~std/compiler:paths {
    vend/pkg: {{ ENTRY }}/lib
}

~import vend/pkg/greet

~vend/pkg/greet:greet()
